(text "RELAY CONTROL. NOT FOR FABRICATION. Finder 40.31.7.012.0000, hand-fitted through-hole.\\nCoil code 7.012: 288 ohm and 42 mA at 12 V from the coil table. Pickup 8.8 V, max 18 V, operate/release 7/3 ms. The family is called 0.65 W; 12 V times 42 mA is 0.50 W.\\nSPDT used as NO. The NC pin is open. UP_COM is not tied to DN_COM. Neither contact pin touches GND.\\nThe Finder DC1 rating is 10 A resistive at 30 V. That rating is not the Lofrans contactor load and is not the track size.\\nContact copper is calculated for a provisional 2 A. There is no fuse and no suppressor on the four contact nets. Measure the contactor current and its kick before installation.\\nCoil high side is +12V_COIL, then the external relay-power switch, then the external ignition contact, then R_COILFEED.\\nR_COILFEED is only that series connection. It is not a watchdog bypass. Coil current still has to pass Q_SERIES, and Q_SERIES is on only while the heartbeat is fresh and exactly one direction is requested.\\nBoth GPIOs high: XOR is low, so the AND is low, and each gate is clamped off by the other request.\\nA welded contact is not opened by any of this. There is no auxiliary contact, so the paralleled +12 V node cannot prove which operator closed it." (at 20 265 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))) (uuid "035354bc-6c21-4cbe-94dc-ff998e6ab905"))
