(global_label "COIL_RAIL_OK" (shape passive) (at 309.88 205.74 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "9063af62-5fe1-4876-a99a-2f2a1e631ec5"))
(text "Presence detector: 100k/100k would sit at half the coil rail, so a Schottky to +3V3 clamps the GPIO.\\nAt 12 V the clamp current is about (12-3.6)/100k = 84 uA. At 40 V it is about 0.36 mA. This detects 'rail present', it is not a voltmeter.\\nTimeout: Nexperia tW = K * REXT(kOhm) * CEXT(pF) nanoseconds, K nominal 1 for CEXT above 10 nF. 100k * 3.3 uF = 330 ms typical.\\nLong case, K=1.2 and capacitor +20 percent: about 475 ms. A static level cannot refresh it. Future firmware must edge GPIO1 at least every 100 ms.\\nThe existing prototype firmware does not toggle GPIO1. With that image Q stays low and the coils stay off. Do not modify that firmware.\\nA future image must stop edges and drive both request pins low on STOP, comms loss, an invalid command, or TTL expiry. Those are two separate actions.\\nA stuck-high request with the main loop still running does not hold the coil, because a level on GPIO1 does not retrigger. Edges are allowed only while the RUN is valid.\\nThe run-on after the last legal edge is one pulse: 330 ms typical, about 475 ms long case. Both request pins stuck is still blocked by the XOR.\\nCoil FETs are NX6008NBK: 60 V, RDS max 3 ohm at 2.5 V. Two in series drop about 0.25 V at 42 mA. Flyback is SS14, 1 A, 40 V, across each coil only.\\nThe NO contact is in parallel with the Lofrans and hand controls. The SPDT NC pin is open. Unplugging these contacts leaves the original controls in place.\\nDo not install until the Lofrans control current and its inductive energy are measured and shown to be inside the Finder DC1 figure. DC13 life equals DC1 only if the load already has a diode, which is not assumed." (at 20 100 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))) (uuid "96f16f16-a760-41e2-bc63-cad4798bda78"))
  (embedded_fonts no)
)
